[{:seon.task/name "prove-runs-what-a-change-reaches"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner 2026-10-22: \"why don't we have a comprehensive policy where we are only running tests that have changed?\" (AGENTS.md section 5: results are reused by input digest, unchanged inputs are never run again; section 9: re-running everything on every change). Design: notes/fork-test-merge-design-2026-10-22.md section 2 and its build step 2 (step 1, the reach that sees macros, quoted names and schemas, landed as seon.program/refs-name-quoted-symbols-and-macro-uses). What exists: three selections. (1) `bin/test --reach` (`test-runner/reach-main`) takes `seon.program/reach-digests` over src and test imported as program facts (`test-runner/program-db`), reuses greens stored as <digest>.edn in the shared results directory (`:seon.config.source/test-results-dir`, `test-runner/plan`) and runs the rest serially in its own process (`test-runner/run-vars!`, results written through `seon.fx/write-file`); it is not the default, so `bin/test` runs every deftest (5-8 min). (2) An agent's run (`seon.agent/test-vars`, used by `seon.agent/run-tests-forked` for the turn's observe, the judge's :tested and the gated merge) selects proofs plus `seon.program/reaching-tests` of `seon.program/changed-vars`: only :var/form changes, so a changed method, fixture, ns form or schema selects nothing, and no result is ever reused (task seon.agent/a-wide-reach-stays-cheap: a change to seon.config/value reaches 263 tests, run every turn). (3) `bin/check` runs every step every time; no step is keyed by what it reaches. v1 (~/src/seon seon.test.cache) keyed a test's result by its reach digest and ran only tests without one. The field's way (Bazel, Nix, bors): the action key is the digest of every input; a cached green is the result. Plan, one primitive: `seon.proofs/plan` of a base and a candidate digest map ({key digest}), the green results found at the candidate's digests and the task's proofs answers {:selected :reused :run}: selected is every key whose digest differs from base (or is new), the proofs, and every key with no green at its digest; run is the selected keys with no green at their digest; reused the rest. A key is a test var or a check step: `seon.program/reach-digests` takes the roots to digest (default the db's tests), so a check step's digest is the reach of its mode functions in `seon.proofs/check-steps` (the seon.check function bin/check's step runs) plus the checkout's :env (bin/, native/, resources/, pins: the binary's other inputs), and a step that censuses the whole tree (dragons) takes :tree. Results by digest in the one shared directory: `seon.proofs/greens` reads, `seon.proofs/store!` writes through `seon.fx/write-file` (temp then rename). Runs: tests in `:seon.config.proofs/jobs` forked shards (`seon.proofs/run-shards`: one child per shard of namespaces, each writing its results' lines on a pipe read to EOF, reaped with waitpid; no clock, no thread), check steps through bin/check's own step bodies, named (SEON_CHECK_STEPS), so this changes only which steps run. Front doors: `bin/prove` (tests and check steps; `bin/test` with no namespace and `bin/check` with no argument are it) for lanes and root; `seon.agent/test-vars` selects by `plan` over the agent's base and branch digests and reuses greens, so `seon.agent/run-tests-forked` (observe, :tested, the reconciler's :tests and the merge gate) and `(my.agent/prove)` run only what moved. Full runs are explicit: `bin/test --all`, `bin/check 100`. Replaces: test-runner's plan, run-vars!, reach-main and their green?; test-vars' reaching-tests selection. Deletes `bin/test --reach` (prove is the default). docs/landing.md: a landing runs bin/prove on the merged tree; the full run is daily and before a change to boot, the writer, the reconciler or the build. Done by lane PROVE (2026-10-22), with three changes to the plan the code forced: (a) shards are processes of their own started by bin/test, not forks of the runner: a forked child of the jolt test runtime hangs at its first d/connect (even of the in-memory test store, even after forgetting the parent's connections), so `seon.proofs/shards` deals and `seon.proofs/run-tests!` runs one shard in its process; (b) with a base, plan selects only the proofs and the moved digests (an agent's first turn would otherwise run main's whole suite); without one, also every key with no green; (c) `seon.program/tree-readers` made 327 of 368 tests take the whole tree (a contract expands `seon.config/baked-schema-forms`, which slurps resources/), so any edit reran them: `seon.program/env-readers` names the platform reads of :env inputs. And bin/test builds target/seon whenever anything runs (a test that starts ./seon runs the binary; a root on a binary older than its tree leaves agent vars unbound: task seon.program/loading-a-changed-file-keeps-its-other-vars-bound). Measured: docs/landing.md#a-landing-runs-what-the-change-reaches. Gaps left: an agent's digests take no :env, so its greens are its own, not the shared directory's (the binary's source commit as its :env is next); shards are balanced by test count, not time (time never decides); seon.source-test/a-restart-catches-up-and-a-new-generation-resumes is red on main and its `nc -w 600` never times out an idle connection on macOS, so it holds its shard until its root is killed."
